From 63b8acad3ab3c0de636c0bce918bebd760f09040 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JustFoura <JustFoura.dev@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:26:42 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 02/18] MoE: persistent async fanout pool
 (LLAMA_MOE_FANOUT_ASYNC), GGML_MOE_NODE_LOG phase split,
 GGML_VK_MOE_HOST_MAX_IDS routing knob

- fanout: per-op spawn/join replaced by a persistent pool; ith==0 submits the
  slice list and returns to compute (page-in overlaps compute within and
  across nodes; ring backpressure keeps worker views consistent). Legacy
  spawn/join path kept under LLAMA_MOE_FANOUT_ASYNC=0; forced legacy when
  DONTNEED is on. Kills the ~24-thread create/join storm per mul_mat_id.
- GGML_MOE_NODE_LOG=1: per-node submit/drain/node-wall timestamps exposing the
  IO/compute phase split; revealed the warmup-only execution of the CPU kernel.
- GGML_VK_MOE_HOST_MAX_IDS=N (default -1 = off): rejects wide-id mul_mat_id ops
  whose weights sit in a GPU host buffer so the sched routes them to the CPU
  kernel. Measured discovery behind it: on server prompt paths the sched runs
  ffn_*_exps mul_mat_id on VULKAN (Vulkan_Host-mapped weights streamed through
  uncontrolled GPU page faults, ~0.81 GB/s effective); all CPU-side MoE knobs
  (fanout/DONTNEED/multi-RHS) never executed there. Probe data: request-phase
  MUL_MAT_ID split 147 CPU / 141 Vulkan per graph. CAUTION: at ubatch 16384 the
  CPU-side graph anon buffers OOM the 16 GB machine (kernel killed the desktop
  session 3x); validate at ubatch <= 2048 first.
